# map()/filter() over a list long enough that the mapping function drives
# several collections while the result list is live. Guards two things: every
# result slot holds a real Value from the moment the list becomes reachable,
# and each store into the (by then tenured) result runs the write barrier so
# the nursery objects it points at survive the next minor collection.
xs = range(0, 20000)
ys = map((x) => [x, x * 2], xs)
zs = map((p) => p[1], ys)
ws = filter((p) => p[0] % 2 == 0, ys)
print(len(ys), ys[0], ys[19999])
print(len(zs), zs[12345])
print(len(ws), ws[9999])
